{
    "_comment_": [
        "PE VERSIONINFO resource embedded in smirror.exe (R-24).",
        "",
        "Why: Microsoft Defender's ML classifier flagged the unsigned",
        "smirror.exe v1.0.59 binary as Trojan:Win32/Wacatac.B!ml. One of",
        "the strongest ML signals against us was 'binary has no PE",
        "VERSIONINFO' — anonymous Go builds look like packed/obfuscated",
        "malware. Embedding CompanyName / ProductName / FileVersion /",
        "OriginalFilename in the PE header neutralizes that signal.",
        "",
        "How: edit this file when bumping the version, then regenerate",
        "resource_windows.syso:",
        "",
        "    go install github.com/josephspurrier/goversioninfo/cmd/goversioninfo@latest",
        "    cd cmd/smirror/",
        "    goversioninfo -o resource_windows.syso versioninfo.json",
        "",
        "Go automatically picks up the .syso file on Windows builds and",
        "links the resource into smirror.exe. Verify via:",
        "    smirror.exe → Properties → Details",
        "",
        "Reference: docs/release-maturity.md (R-24);",
        "           docs/operations/wdsi-fp-submission-v1.0.59.md."
    ],
